  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">MCT Program Strategy (2012-2015)</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">MCT Program Strategy (2012-2015)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">MCT is a non statutory national media body that exists to enhance     media profession, code of ethics, influences policies, legislations   and practices in Tanzania. Sweden, Norway, Denmark and Switzerand     supported MCT&apos;s 2007-2011 Programme Strategy. Whereas, only Sweden    Switzerland and Norway will support the 2012-2015.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">MCT &#xe4;r en frivillig sj&#xe4;lvregulerande nationell instans f&#xf6;r att  &#xf6;ka kvaliteten I medierapportering, st&#xe4;rka yrkesetik samt p&#xe5;verka lagstiftning och praxis f&#xf6;r fria medier i Tanzania. Sverige, Norge, Danmark och Switzerand st&#xf6;dde MCT         2007-2011 Program strategi. Sverige, Schweiz och Norge kommer att st&#xf6;dja 2012-2015.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Media Council of Tanzania (MCT) has two overall objectives: 1) to promote freedom of expression and media and 2) t achieve quality in media by promoting quality standards, accountability, social responsibility and skills development.</narrative>
  </description>
